  "title": "SettingsPage save handler sends redundant Content-Type header that authFetch already sets",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: Wiring. Severity: P3. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The handleSaveSettings function passes `headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }` explicitly in the options. However, authFetch (api.ts line 76-78) already auto-adds Content-Type: application/json when a body is present and it's not FormData. This is redundant but harmless. More importantly, this pattern suggests the developer was unsure about authFetch's behavior, which may lead to inconsistency across the codebase where some calls include it and others don't.",
